    "A chemical reaction is really just atoms swapping partners. Nothing is created or destroyed — Lavoisier's Law of Conservation of Mass says the same atoms you started with are still there at the end, just rearranged into new molecules. That's why every equation you balance is a bookkeeping exercise: the number of each atom on the left must equal the number on the right.",
