    "Biomagnification is the dark twin of that same energy math: while *energy* dilutes by 90% at each step, non-biodegradable toxins like DDT don't dilute — they accumulate, because an organism eats many prey over its lifetime and stores the toxin rather than excreting it. That's why a small amount of DDT sprayed on a field ends up most concentrated in the bodies of top predators, who are furthest from the source but eat the most contaminated prey.",
    "Decomposers are easy to overlook because they're small and unglamorous, but they're the hinge the whole cycle turns on: without them, nutrients locked inside dead organisms would never return to the soil, producers would eventually run out of raw materials, and the entire food web above them would collapse — which is why 'decomposers break down dead matter' isn't a side fact, it's the reason ecosystems are cycles rather than one-way streets.",
